msgid "**HTTPS upstream:** ``pveproxy`` speaks only HTTPS, so ``services.proxmox.upstream_scheme: https`` makes the front proxy location reach ``127.0.0.1:7992`` over TLS. The hop stays on the loopback, and nginx does not verify the self-signed ``pveproxy`` certificate. The OAuth2 proxy runs in ``auth_request`` mode and forwards no request to the upstream, so its ``http://proxmox:8006`` upstream entry carries no traffic."
msgstr ""

msgid "**HTTPS upstream:** `pveproxy` speaks only HTTPS, so `services.proxmox.upstream_scheme: https` makes the front proxy location reach `127.0.0.1:7992` over TLS. The hop stays on the loopback, and nginx does not verify the self-signed `pveproxy` certificate. The OAuth2 proxy runs in `auth_request` mode and forwards no request to the upstream, so its `http://proxmox:8006` upstream entry carries no traffic."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**HTTPS** enforced via NGINX reverse proxy."
msgstr "**HTTPS** NGINX alderantzizko proxyaren bidez betearazia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Handler Integration**"
msgstr "**Helduen integrazioa**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Handler Integration**   Restart handler ensures the Docker daemon is reloaded when necessary."
msgstr "**Helduen integrazioa** Berrabiarazi kudeatzaileak Docker daemon-a birkargatzen du beharrezkoa denean."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Handler-safe**: automatically triggers an NGINX reload when templates change."
msgstr "**Kudeatzailea**: automatikoki NGINX birkargatzen du txantiloiak aldatzean."

msgid "**Handlers for Runtime Control:** Automatically builds, sets up, or restarts containers based on handlers. Notify ``compose up`` when rendered files or the service spec changed; notify ``container recreate`` when only in-container or in-database state changed and the process must reload it — the latter force-recreates in compose mode and forces a task recreation in swarm mode, where ``docker stack deploy`` alone would leave the running task untouched. To rebuild and recreate single services while the rest of the stack keeps running, set ``compose_service_up_targets`` to their service keys and notify ``compose-service-up``; it acts in compose mode only and recreates a service only when its image or configuration changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Handlers for Runtime Control:** Automatically builds, sets up, or restarts containers based on handlers. Notify `compose up` when rendered files or the service spec changed; notify `container recreate` when only in-container or in-database state changed and the process must reload it — the latter force-recreates in compose mode and forces a task recreation in swarm mode, where `docker stack deploy` alone would leave the running task untouched. To rebuild and recreate single services while the rest of the stack keeps running, set `compose_service_up_targets` to their service keys and notify `compose-service-up`; it acts in compose mode only and recreates a service only when its image or configuration changed."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Handlers:** Automatic reload/restart of services when definitions change."
msgstr "**Kudeatzaileak:** Zerbitzuen birkarga automatikoa/berrabiapena definizioak aldatzean."

# translated-by: libretranslate
