msgid "**Scrape target:** when ``web-app-prometheus`` is present, the role joins the monitoring closure."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Scrape target:** when `web-app-prometheus` is present, the role joins the monitoring closure."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Script Cloning:** Retrieves the latest swapfile creation script from a Git repository."
msgstr "**Scriptaren klonazioa:** Git biltegi bateko swap-fitxategia sortzeko azken scripta eskuratzen du."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seal is `seal \"static\"`** with a 32-byte key generated by the repo credential generator into the ansible-vault-encrypted inventory and injected as `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`."
msgstr "**Seal dago `seal \"static\"`** a 32-byte gakoa, kredentzial-sortzaileak sortutakoa, ansible-vault-encrypted inbentarioan eta injektatu gisa `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless Collaboration:** Collaborate in real time with team members, ensuring smooth data sharing and project management."
msgstr "**Elkarlan hutsala:** Talde-kideekin denbora errealean lan egin, datu-partekatzea eta proiektuen kudeaketa bermatuz."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless Docker Integration:** Works harmoniously with Docker Compose and other roles in your infrastructure."
msgstr "**Docker-en integrazioa:** Docker Compose-rekin harmonian funtzionatzen du eta zure azpiegiturako beste rol batzuekin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless Docker Integration:** Works with Docker Compose and the central-engine deploy machinery."
msgstr "**Docker-en integrazioa:** Docker Compose-rekin lan egiten du eta motor zentrala erabiltzen du."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless IFrame Embedding**: Launch apps directly within the UI or open in new tabs."
msgstr "**IFrame ez-betegarria**: Abiarazi aplikazioak zuzenean UI barruan edo fitxa berrietan ireki."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless Integration:** Designed to work within a larger system setup environment, integrating with dependencies such as Hunspell for spell checking."
msgstr "**Integrazio motela:** Sistemaren konfigurazio-ingurune handiago batean lan egiteko diseinatua, Hunspell bezalako mendekotasunak uztartuz ortografia-egiaztapena egiteko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless Integration:** Easily integrates with other automation roles for a complete system setup."
msgstr "**Integrazio motela:** Erraz integratzen da beste automatizazio-rol batzuekin sistema osoa konfiguratzeko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless Integration:** Provides a stable and secure browsing setup as part of broader system automation workflows."
msgstr "**Integrazio motela:** Nabigazio-konfigurazio egonkorra eta segurua eskaintzen du sistemaren automatizazio-fluxu zabalagoen barruan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Seamless NGINX Reload:** Reloads the NGINX service automatically after successful renewals."
msgstr "**NGINX Reload:** NGINX zerbitzua automatikoki birkargatzen du ongi berritu ondoren."

msgid "**Search allocation precheck:** [search_allocation_precheck.sh](files/shell/search_allocation_precheck.sh) creates a one-shard probe index named after the container and fails with the answer of `_cluster/allocation/explain`, which names the disk watermark when the data disk is too full, unless Elasticsearch allocates it. `init` runs it in front of `zammad-init`. In compose, the one-shot `precheck` service runs it first and `init` depends on that service, so `compose up` stops on a refusal. Swarm renders no `precheck` service, because `depends_on` does not gate `init` there. Instead the deploy waits until the newest `init` task is `Complete`: a refusing Elasticsearch leaves it `Failed`, the wait stops the deploy, and `docker service logs` of `init` carries the explanation. An `init` the stack deploy did not restart is already `Complete` and passes at once."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Search allocation precheck:** `search_allocation_precheck.sh <files/shell/search_allocation_precheck.sh>`__ creates a one-shard probe index named after the container and fails with the answer of ``_cluster/allocation/explain``, which names the disk watermark when the data disk is too full, unless Elasticsearch allocates it. ``init`` runs it in front of ``zammad-init``. In compose, the one-shot ``precheck`` service runs it first and ``init`` depends on that service, so ``compose up`` stops on a refusal. Swarm renders no ``precheck`` service, because ``depends_on`` does not gate ``init`` there. Instead the deploy waits until the newest ``init`` task is ``Complete``: a refusing Elasticsearch leaves it ``Failed``, the wait stops the deploy, and ``docker service logs`` of ``init`` carries the explanation. An ``init`` the stack deploy did not restart is already ``Complete`` and passes at once."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Search index per Elasticsearch major:** The index lives in a directory named after the Elasticsearch major inside the ``zammad_search`` volume. A new major starts on an empty directory and ``zammad-init`` rebuilds the index from the database on the same deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Search index per Elasticsearch major:** The index lives in a directory named after the Elasticsearch major inside the `zammad_search` volume. A new major starts on an empty directory and `zammad-init` rebuilds the index from the database on the same deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Search, Favourites and Recently Used**: a search field in the header finds every application by title, description, tags and folder names; pinned and recently opened applications sit at the top level."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Search.** It searches applications only, by title, description, tags and folder names, across all folders, live while typing, and shows its hits in a picker with icon, title and folder path."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Second login:** behind the oauth2 gate the render queue still asks for its own login. It accepts the inventory password of the account; a password changed later in Keycloak does not reach it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret hygiene:** Every stored audit payload is passed through ``utils.agents.redact``, so a token, key or password spooled into a note never reaches the chain; the Keycloak and LDAP admin credentials are read from the environment and never logged."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret hygiene:** Every stored audit payload is passed through `utils.agents.redact`, so a token, key or password spooled into a note never reaches the chain; the Keycloak and LDAP admin credentials are read from the environment and never logged."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret path:** The client secret reaches the container base64-encoded on the task's stdin and travels on as an environment variable named by `container exec -e`, so it is never on an argv. Proxmox VE stores it as `client-key` in `/etc/pve/domains.cfg`, where its own `pveum realm add` keeps it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secret path:** The client secret reaches the container base64-encoded on the task’s stdin and travels on as an environment variable named by ``container exec -e``, so it is never on an argv. Proxmox VE stores it as ``client-key`` in ``/etc/pve/domains.cfg``, where its own ``pveum realm add`` keeps it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secrets management with OpenBao.** The new *web-app-openbao* role deploys OpenBao at *openbao.<domain>*. It stores application credentials, API keys and machine identities. People sign in through Keycloak, or through LDAP when OpenLDAP is deployed. Their *administrator*, *operator* or *reader* group decides what they can reach, and signing in without one of those groups grants only the default policy. Services and automation use their own AppRole identities, whose credentials change on every deploy, and no root token is kept after the first deploy. A recovery key kept in the token store lets a later deploy get back in if those credentials are lost. A static seal unseals the node on its own after every restart. An internal PKI can be switched on, and Prometheus alerts when the node is sealed or unreachable. The seal key lives only in the encrypted inventory, and a backup of the store cannot be read without it, so back up the inventory together with the volume. See [web-app-openbao](roles/web-app-openbao/README.md)."
msgstr "**Sekretuen kudeaketarekin OpenBao.** Berria *web-app-openbao* Funtzioa zabaltzea OpenBao at *openbao.<domain>*Aplikazioaren kredentzialak gordetzen ditu, API gakoak eta makina-identitateak. Jendeak sinatu egiten du Keycloakedo LDAP bidez noiz OpenLDAP Zabalduta dago. Haienak *Administratzailea*, *eragilea* edo *irakurlea* Taldeak erabakitzen du zer lor dezaketen, eta talde horietako bat gabe sinatzeak politika lehenetsia baino ez du ematen. Zerbitzuek eta automatizazioak beren AppRole identitate propioak erabiltzen dituzte, kredentzialak aldatu egiten dira hedapen bakoitzean, eta ez da erroko tokenik gordetzen lehen hedapenaren ondoren. Token biltegian gordetako berreskuratze-gako batek aukera ematen du geroago erabiltzeko kredentzialak galduz gero. Zigilu estatiko batek nodoa bere kabuz askatzen du berrabiatu ondoren. Barne PKI bat alda daiteke, eta Prometheus abisuak nodoa zigilatua edo atziezina denean. Zigilu-gakoa inbentario enkriptatuan bakarrik bizi da, eta biltegiaren babeskopia ezin da irakurri hura gabe, beraz, inbentarioa bolumenarekin batera. Ikusi [web-app-openbao](roles/web-app-openbao/README.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secrets reuse the credentials mechanism.** MCP tokens, app-passwords, and OAuth client secrets are declared in each role's [`meta/secrets.yml`](../../roles/web-app-baserow/meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:` block and read via `lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')`. No new secret store is introduced."
msgstr "**Sekretuek kredentzialen mekanismoa berrerabiltzen dute.** MCPren tokenak, aplikazio-pasahitzak eta OAuth bezeroaren sekretuak rol bakoitzean deklaratuak daude [`meta/secrets.yml`](../../roles/web-app-baserow/meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:` blokea eta irakurri bidez `lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')`. Ez dago denda sekretu berririk."

msgid "**Secrets stay out of argv:** forwarded variables reach ``container exec`` by name, their values travel in the environment."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secrets stay out of argv:** forwarded variables reach `container exec` by name, their values travel in the environment."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Access:** Integrates with an NGINX reverse proxy for encrypted, high-performance access."
msgstr "**Sarbide segurua:** NGINX alderantzizko proxy batekin integratzen da, errendimendu handiko sarbide enkriptatua lortzeko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Access:** Utilize NGINX reverse proxy integration to safeguard your management interface."
msgstr "**Sarbide segurua:** Erabili NGINX alderantzizko proxy-integrazioa zure kudeaketa-interfazea babesteko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Communications:** Enable TLS encryption for data in transit when accessed through an NGINX reverse proxy."
msgstr "**Komunikazio seguruak:** Gaitu TLS enkriptazioa bidean dauden datuentzat NGINX alderantzizko proxy baten bidez atzitzean."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Notifications:** Integrates with systemd to trigger email alerts when services fail."
msgstr "**Jakinarazpen seguruak:** Zerbitzuek huts egiten dutenean, abisu elektronikoak aktibatzeko sistematutakoak."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Notifications:** Leverages systemd to trigger alerts automatically when services fail."
msgstr "**Jakinarazpen seguruak:** Leveragesek alerta automatikoki aktibatuko du zerbitzuak huts egiten duenean."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Remote Access:** Facilitates secure remote access by providing a verified public key for use with [SSH](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell)."
msgstr "**Urruneko sarbide segurua:** Urruneko sarbide segurua erraztea gako publiko egiaztatua eskainiz erabiltzeko [SSH](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Remote Access:** Facilitates secure remote access by providing a verified public key for use with `SSH <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell>`__."
msgstr "**Urruneko sarbide segurua:** Urruneko sarbide segurua erraztea gako publiko egiaztatua eskainiz erabiltzeko `SSH <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell>`__."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Reverse Proxy Setup:**"
msgstr "**Alderantzizko proxy seguruaren konfigurazioa:**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Reverse Proxy Setup:**   Easily configure your access through a reverse proxy to ensure secure, controlled entry to your LDAP management tool."
msgstr "**Alderantzizko proxy seguruaren konfigurazioa:** Erraz konfiguratu sarbidea alderantzizko proxy baten bidez LDAP kudeaketa-tresnan sarrera seguru eta kontrolatua bermatzeko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure Web Access:** Configured to work seamlessly behind an NGINX reverse proxy for enhanced security and performance."
msgstr "**Web sarbide segurua:** NGINX alderantzizko proxy baten atzean lan egiteko konfiguratuta, segurtasuna eta errendimendua hobetzeko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure and Private:** Built-in support for TLS, secure SMTP integration, and strict administrative controls to ensure data protection."
msgstr "**Segurua eta pribatua:** TLSren euskarri integratua, SMTPren integrazio segurua eta kontrol administratibo zorrotzak datuen babesa bermatzeko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure and Reliable:** Benefit from secure access via an NGINX reverse proxy combined with a MariaDB backend for reliable data storage."
msgstr "**Segurua eta fidagarria:** Baliatu sarbide segurua NGINX alderantzizko proxy baten bidez, MariaDB motorrarekin konbinatuta datu fidagarriak gordetzeko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure and Scalable:**"
msgstr "**Segurua eta eskalagarria:**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure and Scalable:**   Benefit from container isolation and reproducible deployments that ensure your service is both secure and scalable."
msgstr "**Segurua eta eskalagarria:** Edukiontzien isolamendutik eta zure zerbitzua segurua eta eskalagarria dela ziurtatzen duten hedapen aldagarrietatik etekina atera."

msgid "**Secure boot:** The zfs kernel module of the template is built by DKMS and is not signed, so the agent project's default profile sets `security.secureboot` to `services.incus.agents.secure_boot`, `false` by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Secure boot:** The zfs kernel module of the template is built by DKMS and is not signed, so the agent project’s default profile sets ``security.secureboot`` to ``services.incus.agents.secure_boot``, ``false`` by default."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Secure by Default:** Includes modern SSL headers and best practices via NGINX."
msgstr "**Lehenetsi gisa:** SSL goiburu modernoak eta NGINX bidez praktika onenak sartzen ditu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Security Considerations**: While adding a user to the Docker group provides ease of use, be aware of the security implications. It grants the user elevated privileges which, if misused, can affect the entire system."
msgstr "**Segurtasun-neurriak**: Erabiltzaile bat Docker taldera gehitzeak erabilera erraza ematen duen bitartean, kontuz ibili segurtasun-ondorioez. Erabiltzaileari pribilegio handiak ematen dizkio, eta, gaizki erabiliz gero, sistema osoari eragin diezaioket."

msgid "**Security Defaults:** Disables password authentication and root login; enforces public-key authentication; conditionally sets `LogLevel` to `DEBUG3` when `services.svc-sshd.debug.enabled` is true, which falls back to `DEBUG` via `lookup('debug')`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Security Defaults:** Disables password authentication and root login; enforces public-key authentication; conditionally sets ``LogLevel`` to ``DEBUG3`` when ``services.svc-sshd.debug.enabled`` is true, which falls back to ``DEBUG`` via ``lookup('debug')``."
msgstr ""

