# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The ``mcp`` role is granted per platform, not per application.** A user’s ``roles:`` list carries role names only, and ```build_realm_rbac_groups`` <../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py>`__ matches them without an application context, so ``roles: [mcp]`` makes that user a member of *every* deployed ``/roles/<app>/mcp`` group. Entitling somebody to drive Baserow but not GitLab is therefore not expressible declaratively today; it needs the Keycloak membership to be set directly on the single group. The tool-server side honours whatever membership arrives, so the limit is the platform’s user model, not this wiring, and the Playwright coverage reflects it: it proves “all groups sees all servers” and “no group sees none”, not the selective case."
msgstr "**The ``mcp`` Rola plataformako ematen da, ez aplikazioko.** Erabiltzaile baten izena ``roles:`` Zerrendak rol-izenak bakarrik ditu, eta ```build_realm_rbac_groups`` <../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py>`__ matches them without an application context, so ``roles: [mcp]`` makes that user a member of *every* deployed ``/roles/<app>/mcp`` taldea. Norbait gidatzen Baserow baina ez GitLab Beraz, gaur ez da adierazgarria; behar du. Keycloak talde bakar bateko kide izatea. Tresna-zerbitzariak edozein kideri ohore egiten dio, beraz, muga plataformaren erabiltzaile-eredua da, ez adarkatze hori, eta Playwright-en estaldurak islatzen du: \"talde guztiek zerbitzari guztiak ikusten dituzte\" eta \"taldek ez du bat ere ikusten\", ez selektiboa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The `mcp` role is granted per platform, not per application.** A user's `roles:` list carries role names only, and [`build_realm_rbac_groups`](../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py) matches them without an application context, so `roles: [mcp]` makes that user a member of *every* deployed `/roles/<app>/mcp` group. Entitling somebody to drive Baserow but not GitLab is therefore not expressible declaratively today; it needs the Keycloak membership to be set directly on the single group. The tool-server side honours whatever membership arrives, so the limit is the platform's user model, not this wiring, and the Playwright coverage reflects it: it proves \"all groups sees all servers\" and \"no group sees none\", not the selective case."
msgstr "**The `mcp` Rola plataformako ematen da, ez aplikazioko.** Erabiltzaile baten izena `roles:` Zerrendak rol-izenak bakarrik ditu, eta [`build_realm_rbac_groups`](../web-app-keycloak/filter_plugins/build_realm_rbac_groups.py) aplikazio-testuingururik gabe bat datoz. `roles: [mcp]` erabiltzaile horrek kide egiten du *bakoitza* hedatua `/roles/<app>/mcp` taldea. Baserow gidatzeko norbait bultzatzea, baina ez GitLab, beraz, ez da gaur egun argi eta garbi azaltzen; Keycloak-eko kide izatea behar du talde bakarrean zuzenean ezartzeko. Tresna-zerbitzariak edozein kideri ohore egiten dio, beraz, muga plataformaren erabiltzaile-eredua da, ez hariketa hori, eta Playwright-en estaldurak islatzen du: \"talde guztiek zerbitzari guztiak ikusten dituzte\" eta \"inork ez du ikusten\"Ez kasu selektiboa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The adapter leaked its upstream credential on a redirect.** It opened the upstream with `urlopen`, which follows redirects, and urllib copies the original request's headers onto the target, so an upstream answering `302` with an off-host location would have handed the credential to whoever it named. The opener now refuses redirects outright, since the target is contracted."
msgstr "**Egokitzaileak korrontearen kredentziala birbideratu zuen.** Honek korrontea ireki zuen. `urlopen`, birbideratzeak jarraitzen dituena, eta urllib-ek jatorrizko eskaeraren goiburuak kopiatzen ditu helburura, beraz, ibaian gora erantzuten du. `302` ostatuz kanpoko kokaleku batek kredentziala emango zion izendatu duenari. Orain irekitzaileak uko egiten dio birzuzenketari, helburua kontratatuta dagoelako."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The agent then runs autonomously, step by step:**"
msgstr "**Orduan, agenteak modu autonomoan egiten du lan, urratsez urrats:**"

msgid "**The alias is the switch.** `services.litellm.router.alias` defaults to `auto`; setting it empty publishes no route and renders no `callbacks` entry, so the hook is not even a condition of starting the proxy. One knob, because a separate enable flag would let `services.yml` read as on while the router is off."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The app volumes are really discarded** (`down --volumes`) and re-created empty by `compose create`, so what comes back can only come from the backup. The database projects go down without `--volumes` on purpose: their data directory carries the database itself, which the deploy creates and the container does not, so a wiped datadir would leave `baudolo-restore --empty -d <db>` with nothing to connect to. The database half loses no proof by it — the pre-clean drops the schema including the marker table, and only the dump brings it back."
msgstr "**Aplikazioaren bolumenak baztertu egiten dira.** (`down --volumes`) eta berriro sortu zen hutsik `compose create`, Itzultzen dena babeskopiatik bakarrik etor daiteke. Datu-basearen proiektuak jaitsi egiten dira. `--volumes` helburuz: datu-direktorioak datu-basea bera du, eta horrek sortzen du eta edukiontziak ez, beraz, ezabatutako datu-dir batek utziko luke. `baudolo-restore --empty -d <db>` Ezerekin konektatzeko. Datu-basearen erdiak ez du inolako frogarik galtzen; pre-garbiak eskema bertan behera uzten du, markatzaileen taula barne, eta dump-ak bakarrik itzultzen du."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The axes are part of a row's identity.** They appear in the job label as glyphs, in the plan table as columns, and in the artifact name. Two rows that differ only in distro are two deploys and MUST NOT share an artifact name."
msgstr "**Ardatzak errenkada baten identitatearen zati dira.** Lan-etiketan glyphs gisa agertzen dira, plan-taulan zutabe gisa, eta objektu-izenean. Distroan bakarrik bereizten diren bi errenkada bi biderketa dira eta ez dute izen artifizialik partekatu behar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-format
msgid "**The axes are selectable.** `%distro` and `/filesystem` narrow a `whitelist` or `priority` token the same way `@mode` and `+tor` do. A retrigger reads the distro back off a failed job's title, so a red row returns on the distribution it died on. It does not read the filesystem back: the title states the kind the matrix assigned, which a deploy may have fallen back from, and writing it into a token would state it as named by a human and make it binding."
msgstr "**Ardatzak hautagarriak dira.** `%distro` eta `/filesystem` estua `whitelist` edo `priority` token berdin `@mode` eta `+tor` Egizu. Atzera-grabatzaile batek huts egindako lanaren titulua irakurtzen du, eta, beraz, errenkada gorri bat itzultzen da hil zen banaketan. Ez du fitxategi-sistema atzera irakurtzen: tituluak adierazten du zein matrize-motari esleitu zaion, zeinetatik adats bat erori den, eta token batean idazteak gizaki batek izendatu eta lotuko luke."

msgid "**The cache is one store, and it is the database the gateway already needs.** A translation is cached on the tuple of engine, source language, target language and the digest of the source text. No second cache technology is introduced for it; a Redis consumer declaration stays off unless a measurement shows the database cache is the bottleneck."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The consumers must be down.** `--empty` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates the schema in between and the dump's own `CREATE TABLE` then fails. The replay checks the consumer's compose project and refuses while anything of it runs."
msgstr "**Kontsumitzaileak jaitsi egin behar dira.** `--empty` eskema psql saio batean garbitu eta hurrengo batean jokatzen du; kontsumitzaile abioko batek eskema birsortzen du eta irauliaren berarena. `CREATE TABLE` gero huts egiten du. Erreproduzitzeak kontsumitzailearen konposaketa-proiektua egiaztatzen du, eta uko egiten dio ezer gertatzen den bitartean."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The consumers must be down.** ``--empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays in the next; a booting consumer recreates the schema in between and the dump’s own ``CREATE TABLE`` then fails. The replay checks the consumer’s compose project and refuses while anything of it runs."
msgstr "**Kontsumitzaileak jaitsi egin behar dira.** ``--empty`` eskema psql saio batean garbitu eta hurrengo batean jokatzen du; abio-kontsumitzaile batek eskema birsortzen du eta zabortegiaren berarena. ``CREATE TABLE`` gero huts egiten du. Erreproduzitzeak kontsumitzailearen konposaketa-proiektua egiaztatzen du, eta uko egiten dio ezer gertatzen den bitartean."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The decision is deterministic, and a learned decision model is out of scope.** Among the routes that survive the filter, each is scored on the factors of decision 9 and the highest scorer wins, with the alias breaking a tie. The same request therefore returns the same model twice. No inference runs, nothing is downloaded, and the CI rows mean the same thing as production."
msgstr "**Erabaki determinista da, eta erabaki-eredu ikasia ez dago eskura.** Iragazkitik bizirik irauten duten bideen artean, bakoitzak erabaki-faktoreak jasotzen ditu. 9 eta puntuaziorik altuenak irabazten du, aliasak gorbata hautsiz. Beraz, eskaera berberak bi aldiz ematen du eredu bera. Ez da inferentziarik exekutatzen, ez da ezer deskargatzen, eta CI errenkadak produkzioaren gauza bera dira."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The deploy can create a role-internal administrator.** On an instance with no users at all there is no OIDC administrator to borrow an API key from, so [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) creates the `openwebui-api-bot` declared in [`meta/users.yml`](./meta/users.yml), whose password the platform generates with every other user's. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` disabled and refuses an OIDC login whose email a local account already holds, so seeding a person's address would lock them out of their own login. On an instance that already has an administrator no account is created."
msgstr "**Hedapenak rol barneko administratzaile bat sor dezake.** Kasu batean, erabiltzailerik gabe, ez dago OIDC administratzailerik API gako bat maileguan hartzeko. [`tasks/utils/mcp.yml`](./tasks/utils/mcp.yml) sortzen du `openwebui-api-bot` deklaratuta [`meta/users.yml`](./meta/users.yml), Plataformak beste erabiltzaile guztiekin sortzen duen pasahitza. Ez da nahita OIDC identitatea: Open WebUI ontziak `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` desgaituta eta uko egiten dio OIDC-ren saio-hasiera bati, kontu lokal batek jadanik duen posta elektronikoari, beraz, pertsona baten helbideak bere saio-hasieratik blokeatuko lituzke. Dagoeneko administratzaile bat duen kasu batean ez da konturik sortzen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The deploy can create a role-internal administrator.** On an instance with no users at all there is no OIDC administrator to borrow an API key from, so ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates the ``openwebui-api-bot`` declared in ```meta/users.yml`` <./meta/users.yml>`__, whose password the platform generates with every other user’s. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships ``OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`` disabled and refuses an OIDC login whose email a local account already holds, so seeding a person’s address would lock them out of their own login. On an instance that already has an administrator no account is created."
msgstr "**Hedapenak rol barneko administratzaile bat sor dezake.** Kasu batean, erabiltzailerik gabe, ez dago OIDC administratzailerik API gako bat maileguan hartzeko. ```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates the ``openwebui-api-bot`` declared in ```meta/users.yml`` <./meta/users.yml>`__, whose password the platform generates with every other user’s. It is deliberately not an OIDC identity: Open WebUI ships ``OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`` desgaituta eta uko egiten dio OIDC-ren saio-hasiera bati, kontu lokal batek jadanik duen posta elektronikoari, beraz, pertsona baten helbideak bere saio-hasieratik blokeatuko lituzke. Dagoeneko administratzaile bat duen kasu batean ez da konturik sortzen."

msgid "**The embedded PostgreSQL pins the plain ``postgres`` image** — the platform’s postgis default defeats baudolo’s substring database detection and would degrade backups to torn live-file snapshots. ``backup.project_hard_restart`` brings the whole project back through one coherent restart after baudolo’s per-volume stop/start cycles."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The embedded PostgreSQL pins the plain `postgres` image** — the platform's postgis default defeats baudolo's substring database detection and would degrade backups to torn live-file snapshots. `backup.project_hard_restart` brings the whole project back through one coherent restart after baudolo's per-volume stop/start cycles."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The engine is read, not guessed.** It comes from the service key in the consuming role's `meta/services.yml`, the same value that fed the backup seed, resolved through `utils/recovery/databases.py`. A dump whose engine no role claims aborts the run instead of being replayed with an assumption."
msgstr "**Motorra irakurria dago, ez asmatua.** Zerbitzu-gakotik dator, kontsumo-funtzioan. `meta/services.yml`, Babeskopia-hazia elikatzen zuen balio bera. `utils/recovery/databases.py`. Hondakin bat, zeinaren motorrak ez duen inolako betebeharrik, exekuzioa bertan behera uzten duen, suposizio baten ordez."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The engine is read, not guessed.** It comes from the service key in the consuming role’s ``meta/services.yml``, the same value that fed the backup seed, resolved through ``utils/recovery/databases.py``. A dump whose engine no role claims aborts the run instead of being replayed with an assumption."
msgstr "**Motorra irakurria dago, ez asmatua.** Zerbitzu-gakotik dator, kontsumo-funtzioan. ``meta/services.yml``, Babeskopia-hazia elikatzen zuen balio bera. ``utils/recovery/databases.py``. Hondakin bat, zeinaren motorrak ez duen inolako betebeharrik, exekuzioa bertan behera uzten duen, suposizio baten ordez."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The file's content IS the value of `applications.<app>.<topic>`. There is NO wrapping key matching the filename.**"
msgstr "**Fitxategiaren edukia balioa da `applications.<app>.<topic>`. Ez dago fitxategi-izenarekin bat datorren bilgarri-gakorik.**"

msgid "**The gateway is a new role, `web-svc-translate`, published at `api.translate.{{ DOMAIN_PRIMARY }}`.** It is not an extension of `web-svc-libretranslate`, because that role publishes one engine's own API and SSO-protected frontend, and a router in front of several engines is a different responsibility with its own database and its own failure modes."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The gateway is authenticated with per-consumer virtual keys.** LiteLLM virtual keys are issued per consumer (OpenWebUI, Flowise, and each 032 agent); a master key is admin-only. This gives per-consumer rate limiting and revocation. The gateway MUST NOT be reachable unauthenticated even on the internal overlay. Keys live in each consumer role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block."
msgstr "**Sarbidea gako birtualekin autentifikatuta dago.** LiteLLM gako birtualak kontsumitzaile bakoitzeko igortzen dira (OpenWebUI, Flowise eta bakoitza 032 agentea); Gako nagusia administratzea da soilik. Honek kontsumo-tasaren mugapena eta errebokatzea ematen du. Atebidea ez da atez atekoa izan behar barneko gainjartzean ere. Gakoak kontsumitzaile bakoitzaren funtzioetan bizi dira `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` blokea."

msgid "**The gateway speaks the LibreTranslate API.** `POST /translate`, `POST /detect` and `GET /languages` keep their published request and response shapes. A consumer therefore points at the gateway by changing one URL, and anything that already speaks to LibreTranslate works unchanged. The gateway is a router, not a new dialect."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The head leads unless an operator says otherwise.** Chunk 0 starts at the top of the ranking. The list is ordered coverage-first, so its head is what a run most needs proven, and a sweep that cannot afford the whole list leaves the tail behind rather than sliding a window over it."
msgstr "**Buruak gidatuko du, operadoreak bestela esaten ez badu.** Chunk 0 rankingaren goialdean hasten da. Zerrenda estaldura ordenatua da lehenik, beraz, bere burua da beharrik gehien erakutsi duena, eta zerrenda osoa ordaindu ezin duen miaketa batek isatsa uzten du leiho bat gainetik irristatu ordez."

msgid "**The heavy backends live in separate variants.** LTEngine and Ollama are not enabled in the same variant, and the variant set is measured with `cli/meta/roles/applications/ressources` against the budget before the matrix runs."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The hook ships as a mounted Python file, not a derived image.** LiteLLM's `proxy_server.py` resolves a custom handler through `get_instance_fn(value, config_file_path)`, which loads `module.instance` out of the directory holding `config.yaml`. A `.py` file rendered next to it is therefore imported at proxy start with no image change, and `services.litellm.image` stays on its pin. [`probe_auth.py`](../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/files/python/probe_auth.py) is the precedent for a Python file the role ships and the container runs."
msgstr "**Koma-ontziak muntatutako Python fitxategi gisa, ez irudi eratorri bat.** LiteLLM-ren `proxy_server.py` Kudeatzaile pertsonalizatu bat konpontzen du `get_instance_fn(value, config_file_path)`, kargatzen duena `module.instance` direktoriotik kanpo `config.yaml`. A `.py` Beraz, proxy-aren hasieran inportatu egiten da irudi aldaketarik gabe, eta `services.litellm.image` Jarri bere pinean. [`probe_auth.py`](../../roles/svc-ai-litellm/files/python/probe_auth.py) Python fitxategi baten aurrekaria da rol-ontziak eta edukiontziak exekutatzen dira."

msgid "**The integration matrix is a generated artifact with a sanctioned generator.** The generator is a [docs-build generator](../../roles/web-app-docs/files/python/infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py) that emits its pages on every docs build, so no copy is committed and none can drift. It MUST satisfy the repo lints: it stays under the 500-line limit, it uses the shared project-root helper instead of a local `__file__` upward walk, and it carries no self-path literal or `requirement NNN` token. It derives every edge from the repository, so a dead upstream URL cannot outlive the declaration it came from."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The integration matrix is the cross-role addon backlog.** The role×role capability map is generated on every docs build by [infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py](../../roles/web-app-docs/files/python/infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py) and reached from [docs/architecture/integrations.rst](../architecture/integrations.rst); [027-integration-matrix.md](027-integration-matrix.md) states where an integration's truth lives and which ones are still open. **Wired** edges are integrations already active through an infinito-native service flag in the row role's `meta/services.yml` (e.g. `sso`→keycloak, `matomo`, `prometheus`, `email`→mailu), derived by scanning the repository, no action required. **Declared** edges are upstream app↔app plugins wired as addons. **Open** edges are verified upstream plugins that nothing declares yet, the backlog this requirement commits to wire. **Paid** edges are the same as open but gated behind a commercial tier (opt-in, operator-enabled). No committed copy of the map exists to drift, so there is nothing to regenerate by hand; the `meta/addons/` migrations move an edge from open to declared over time."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The job proves the machine before it deploys.** [assert_architecture.sh](../../../scripts/github/runner/assert_architecture.sh) compares `uname -m` against the assigned value and fails the row on a mismatch. Without it, a label that stops resolving to arm64 hardware would report every arm64 row green from an amd64 machine, which is the exact failure the axis exists to rule out."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "**The learning log is a `History`-shaped table in the gateway's own database**, one row per offered engine per decision, each row marking whether that engine won. The signature groups comparable requests: source language, target language, and a coarse content class derived from the payload's length and whether it carries markup. `wins(signature)` returns `{engine: (won, seen)}` and feeds decision 5's criteria line, so the next decision reads what earlier ones concluded. A log that cannot be read MUST degrade to deciding without it and MUST NOT fail the request."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The mail provider is a service, not a role name.** Stalwart declares *provides: email* and Mailu *covers: [email]*. The new *mail_provider* lookup returns the configured provider while it is deployed, otherwise the first deployed role offering *email*, and reads the cluster-wide groups so swarm workers agree with the manager. The port-collision lint accepts a collision only inside a registry-declared provider-alternative group, and a new lint fails every role that reads the *email* lookup without emitting *container_extra_hosts*."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The matrix carries the runner label, and `runs-on` reads it.** The entry gains `architecture` and `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) owns the mapping (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`). An architecture without a label is a build error rather than a row that lands on the wrong hardware with an empty `runs-on`."
msgstr "**Matrizeak korrikalariaren etiketa darama, eta `runs-on` irakurri.** Sarrerak irabazten du `architecture` eta `runner`; [pools.py](../../../utils/github/variant/pools.py) mapaketaren jabea da (`amd64` → `ubuntu-latest`, `arm64` → `ubuntu-24.04-arm`)Etiketarik gabeko arkitektura eraikuntza-errorea da, okerreko hardwarean hutsik dagoen errenkada bat baino. `runs-on`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The migration is blocked on a transport gap, and the credential half of it is already built.** The adapter presented its upstream credential only as a header (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) while Baserow keys its endpoint by URL segment, so `policy.upstream_url` now splices an optional `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` and `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` into the upstream URL, delivered through the same `upstream.env` file. With neither variable set it returns the base URL unchanged, which is why the fourteen existing providers are untouched."
msgstr "**Migrazioa blokeatuta dago garraio-hutsune batean, eta kredentzialaren erdia egina dago jadanik.** Egokitzaileak bere korrontearen kredentziala goiburu gisa bakarrik aurkeztu zuen. (`ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_KEY` → `Authorization: Bearer …`) Baserow-k bere amaierako puntua URL segmentuaren bidez ezartzen duen bitartean, beraz, `policy.upstream_url` orain aukerako bat ematen du `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_KEY` eta `ADAPTER_UPSTREAM_PATH_SUFFIX` igotako URLra, bide beretik bidalita `upstream.env` fitxategia. Aldagai-multzorik gabe, oinarrizko URLa itzultzen du aldatu gabe, eta horregatik daude hamalau hornitzaileak ukitu gabe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The platform does not deploy one all-powerful OpenAPI-to-MCP process.** It provides one reusable, immutable adapter implementation and instantiates it once per provider application or per equally isolated trust domain. Each instance attaches only to the provider's own network, receives only that provider's least-privileged credential, exposes a distinct endpoint, and stays addressable by the provider's `application_id`. Every exposed provider remains a separate logical MCP server even when a common implementation serves it, which preserves the mapping between `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`, the client connection, the upstream credential, the tool allowlist and the audit record."
msgstr "**Plataformak ez du OpenAPI-to-MCP prozesu indartsurik hedatzen.** Egokitzaile berrerabilgarri eta aldaezin bat eskaintzen du, eta hornitzaile-aplikazioko edo fidagarritasun-domeinu isolatukoko aldi berean aktibatzen du. instantzia bakoitza hornitzailearen sareari bakarrik eransten zaio, hornitzailearen kredentzial pribilegiatua bakarrik jasotzen du, amaierako puntu bat erakusten du, eta hornitzailearen helbideak mantentzen ditu. `application_id`. Emandako hornitzaile bakoitzak MCP zerbitzari logikoa izaten jarraitzen du inplementazio komun batek balio duenean ere, eta horrek mapatzea mantentzen du bien artean. `roles/<provider-application-id>/mcp`, Bezeroaren konexioa, korrontearen kredentziala, tresnaren baimen-zerrenda eta auditoria-erregistroa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The pools are narrowable per run.** The `distros` and `filesystem` inputs default to empty, which means every declared value. Narrowing is for chasing one distribution or one filesystem."
msgstr "**Igerilekuak estugarriak dira korrikako.** The `distros` eta `filesystem` sarrera hutsak, balio deklaratu guztiak esan nahi du. Narrowing banaketa edo fitxategi-sistema baten atzetik ibiltzea da."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The raft volume is `nfs: false` and the service carries `placement: manager`.**"
msgstr "**Baltsaren bolumena da `nfs: false` eta zerbitzuak eramaten du `placement: manager`.**"

msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** ``bao operator init`` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through ``sys-token-store`` (``DIR_SECRETS``, backed up, and it survives both ``RESET`` and a replaced manager, each of which takes ``.applied.json`` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, ``tasks/utils/recover.yml`` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The recovery key is the way back in.** `bao operator init` issues it once and nothing reissues it, which is what makes it useful — it is the only authority here that does not rotate. It is persisted through `sys-token-store` (`DIR_SECRETS`, backed up, and it survives both `RESET` and a replaced manager, each of which takes `.applied.json` with it). When neither the inventory AppRole nor the recorded one is accepted, `tasks/utils/recover.yml` mints a root token from it and re-pins the AppRole. It cannot decrypt the store — only the seal key can — so it is not a substitute for backing up the inventory."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The role network's gateway is never banned** (`STALWART_ALLOWED_IPS`, an `x:AllowedIp` entry): every container that reaches the published ports through the host arrives from that address."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The role network’s gateway is never banned** (``STALWART_ALLOWED_IPS``, an ``x:AllowedIp`` entry): every container that reaches the published ports through the host arrives from that address."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The role tree is the audit.** Every fact about a role's MCP surface lives in its own `meta/services.yml`; no separate artifact duplicates it."
msgstr "**Rol-zuhaitza ikuskaritza da.** Rol baten gainazalaren inguruko egitate bakoitza bere baitan bizi da `meta/services.yml`; ez du artefaktu bereizirik bikoizten."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The router is a LiteLLM pre-call hook, not a semantic router.** The hook summarizes the request, filters the gateway's own model list down to the routes that can serve it, and picks one. LiteLLM's built-in `auto_router` is explicitly rejected: it routes by embedding similarity to example utterances, which answers \"what is this about\" rather than \"which model can serve this\", and it pulls in the `semantic-router` extra plus an embedding backend the gateway does not otherwise need."
msgstr "**Bideratzailea LiteLLM aurredeiko kako bat da, ez bideratzaile semantikoa.** Gakoak eskaera laburbiltzen du, atebidearen ereduen zerrenda iragazten du, eta bat hartzen du. LiteLLM barruan dago `auto_router` Esplizituki baztertzen da: hitz adibideen antzekotasuna txertatuz doa, eta horrek erantzuten du \"Zer da hau?\" ordez, \"zein modelok erabil dezakeen hau\"eta tira egiten dio. `semantic-router` atebideak ez du besterik behar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The router is an alias beside the default, and it fails loud.** The gateway publishes one additional `model_name` (`auto`). `LITELLM_CHAT_MODEL` and every existing alias keep resolving exactly as they do today, and a consumer opts in by naming `auto`."
msgstr "**Bideratzailea alias bat da lehenespenez, eta zarata egiten du.** Atebideak beste bat argitaratzen du `model_name` (`auto`). `LITELLM_CHAT_MODEL` eta existitzen diren alias guztiek gaur egun egiten duten bezala erabakitzen dute, eta kontsumitzaileak aukeratzen du izendatuz. `auto`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The ``static`` seal wraps the raft root key with ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, injected as ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned ``rotatable: false``: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` then emits the ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Zigiluaren gakoa joko osoa da.** The ``static`` zigiluak baltsamaren erroko gakoa biltzen du ``secrets.credentials.seal_key``, Injektatu honela ``env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY``. raft bolumenaren babeskopia bat da **deszifratu gabe**eta ``svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`` Ez du estaltzen, enkriptatutako inbentarioa da bere etxe bakarra, beraz, berreskuratu inbentarioa horren arabera. Pintatzen da ``rotatable: false``: Zigilu estatikoak belaunaldi bat darama, eta deploy bakoitzak belaunaldi ezkutu bat berreskuraezina bihurtzen du. Biratu nahita inbentarioaren balioa aldatuz; ``openbao.hcl.j2`` gero igortzen du ``previous_key``/``previous_key_id`` bikotea, nodoa giltza zaharrarekin askatzen da eta berrira itzultzen da."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The seal key is the whole ballgame.** The `static` seal wraps the raft root key with `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, injected as `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. A backup of the raft volume is **undecryptable without it**, and `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` does not cover it — the encrypted inventory is its only home, so back the inventory up accordingly. It is pinned `rotatable: false`: the static seal carries one generation of slack, and spending that every deploy makes any skipped generation unrecoverable. Rotate it deliberately by changing the inventory value; `openbao.hcl.j2` then emits the `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` pair, the node unseals with the old key and rewraps to the new one."
msgstr "**Zigiluaren gakoa joko osoa da.** The `static` zigiluak baltsamaren erroko gakoa biltzen du `secrets.credentials.seal_key`, Injektatu honela `env://OPENBAO_SEAL_KEY`. raft bolumenaren babeskopia bat da **deszifratu gabe**eta `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local` Ez du estaltzen, enkriptatutako inbentarioa da bere etxe bakarra, beraz, berreskuratu inbentarioa horren arabera. Pintatzen da `rotatable: false`: Zigilu estatikoak belaunaldi bat darama, eta deploy bakoitzak belaunaldi ezkutu bat berreskuraezina bihurtzen du. Biratu nahita inbentarioaren balioa aldatuz; `openbao.hcl.j2` gero igortzen du `previous_key`/`previous_key_id` bikotea, nodoa giltza zaharrarekin askatzen da eta berrira itzultzen da."

msgid "**The shared mechanism is extracted, not duplicated.** `Sampler`, `History`, `record_of`, `judge_answers` and `decide` move into one Python package owned by `svc-ai-s1`, which owns the decider contract, and staged into both `svc-ai-litellm` and `web-svc-translate` the way the MCP adapter's build context is staged per instance. The model router's behaviour MUST not change: its existing tests are the regression net for the extraction."
msgstr ""

msgid "**The strategy derives from the deployment, not from a hand-set value.** `services.translate.router.strategy` follows `services.s1.enabled`: with the decider deployed the gateway asks it, and without it the gateway falls to a `preference` strategy it can compute itself from a declared engine order. One path leads from the deployment to the behaviour."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**The version has to fit.** The dump states which server it came out of, in its own header — `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` for postgres, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` for mariadb. That is compared against the running engine before the pre-clean touches anything. Restoring forward across a major version is the upgrade path and stays allowed; backward is refused, because a newer dump uses syntax an older server rejects and the schema would already be dropped by then. The version is deliberately not kept in `databases.csv`: that file is written at seed time and would state the version deployed back then, not the one the dump came from — and a generation copied to another host carries its header along, a csv row does not."
msgstr "**Bertsioa egokitu behar da.** Zabortegiak adierazten du zein zerbitzaritatik irten zen, bere goiburuan: `-- Dumped from database version 17.11` postgreserako, `-- Server version\\t11.8.8-MariaDB` mariadbentzat. Motorrarekin konparatzen da, aurreko garbiketak ezer ukitu aurretik. Bertsio nagusi batetik aurrera leheneratzea bertsio-berritze-bidea da, eta atzera egitea onartzen da, beste iraulketa batek sintaxia erabiltzen duelako zerbitzari zaharrago bati uko egiten diolako eta eskema bertan behera utziko litzatekeelako. Bertsioa ez dago nahita gordeta. `databases.csv`: Fitxategi hori hazi-denboran idatzita dago, eta orduan adieraziko luke bertsioa hedatua dagoela, eta ez iraulitakoa, eta beste ostalari bati kopiatutako belaunaldi batek bere goiburua darama, CSV errenkadak ez."

