msgid "**Translation memory:** every approved string is reusable by the gateway and by other components."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Translation quality is judged against the source, not only against the catalogue.** Echo, collapse and a damaged protected span are visible in the catalogue alone; a fluent translation that means something else is not. A `score` question to the decider, carrying the source text, the translation and the file the entry came from, places each sampled entry on an ordered scale from \"says something different\" to \"carries the source faithfully\". Anything the decider places below the middle level is a finding, named with its catalogue, its entry and its file, because a silent wrong translation is the failure this whole requirement exists to prevent."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Translation**, wall-clock and throughput only: `INFINITO_I18N_LANES` and `INFINITO_I18N_BATCH_SIZE` in `.env`. This skill measures around the `i18n-*` targets and never runs them, never changes engine selection and never edits a prompt. Engine choice dominates throughput, because a specialized MT model on the GPU beats an LLM for bulk translation by a wide margin, so a dead engine is a performance defect and not only a gap — report that to the routine which owns those targets and settles quality against a per-language benchmark."
msgstr ""

