msgid "A deploy whose store guard finds a 0.16 store migrates it on its own ([`tasks/store_guard/migrate.yml`](tasks/store_guard/migrate.yml)): it stages `migrate-v016/migrate.sh` in the role's instance directory (`STALWART_MIGRATE_SCRIPT`, a copy of [`files/shell/migrate_v016.sh`](files/shell/migrate_v016.sh)), the values it reads in `migrate.env` ([`templates/migrate.env.j2`](templates/migrate.env.j2)) and the target configuration, runs the phases below from `upgrade` to `final`, reads the store layout again and deploys Stalwart 1.x on the migrated store. Mail is down from the stop in `final` until the deploy starts 1.x. A failing phase stops the deploy with the 0.16 store and server back in place. The deploy runs the script as an async job and polls it every `STALWART_MIGRATE_ASYNC_POLL` seconds, so a dropped SSH connection does not end the deploy; after `STALWART_MIGRATE_ASYNC_TIME` seconds (6 h, scaled by `TIMEOUT_FACTOR`) Ansible kills the script and fails the deploy, while a `stalwart-migrate` container it started keeps running and Stalwart stays stopped when the kill hits `final`. Every phase but `status` and `report` takes `migrate-v016/migrate.lock` and stops at once while another run holds it or a `stalwart-migrate` container still runs. The phases also run by hand, as root:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A deploy whose store guard finds a 0.16 store migrates it on its own (```tasks/store_guard/migrate.yml`` <tasks/store_guard/migrate.yml>`__): it stages ``migrate-v016/migrate.sh`` in the role’s instance directory (``STALWART_MIGRATE_SCRIPT``, a copy of ```files/shell/migrate_v016.sh`` <files/shell/migrate_v016.sh>`__), the values it reads in ``migrate.env`` (```templates/migrate.env.j2`` <templates/migrate.env.j2>`__) and the target configuration, runs the phases below from ``upgrade`` to ``final``, reads the store layout again and deploys Stalwart 1.x on the migrated store. Mail is down from the stop in ``final`` until the deploy starts 1.x. A failing phase stops the deploy with the 0.16 store and server back in place. The deploy runs the script as an async job and polls it every ``STALWART_MIGRATE_ASYNC_POLL`` seconds, so a dropped SSH connection does not end the deploy; after ``STALWART_MIGRATE_ASYNC_TIME`` seconds (6 h, scaled by ``TIMEOUT_FACTOR``) Ansible kills the script and fails the deploy, while a ``stalwart-migrate`` container it started keeps running and Stalwart stays stopped when the kill hits ``final``. Every phase but ``status`` and ``report`` takes ``migrate-v016/migrate.lock`` and stops at once while another run holds it or a ``stalwart-migrate`` container still runs. The phases also run by hand, as root:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A deploy with the mail provider switched off starts the local postfix relay on `127.0.0.1:25` (`tasks/enable.yml:37`), but a mail server an earlier deploy started on the same host keeps running and publishes port 25 (and 465) on `0.0.0.0`, so postfix fails with `fatal: bind 127.0.0.1 port 25: Address already in use` and the deploy stops at \"Ensure the local relay is listening\". Measured in the IAM B2 compose round of 2026-11-01 with `web-app-stalwart` left running from the previous round (`/tmp/compose-deploy-iam-18.log:64181`); the same holds on a production host that switches email off after running Stalwart, because the app-control of the new round does not cover the old provider (`app-control stop web-app-stalwart` answers \"not under app control\"). Options: before starting postfix, detect a listener on port 25 and fail with a message naming the running mail server and how to stop it, or stop the previous provider's stack when its application leaves the inventory. Tracked in issue #1333."
msgstr ""

