# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A single wildcard replaces 15+ per-shape entries (`* make *`, `docker *`, `gh api *`, `grep *`, `head *`, `tail *`, `tee *`, `wc *`, `echo *`, `pkill *`, `* > /tmp/*`, `*=* python* *`, `gh issue *`, `gh run *`, `make *`) that existed purely as workarounds for the sandbox auto-allow heuristic declining on env-prefixes, redirects, pipes, and quoted args. With `Bash(*)` the allowlist no longer rots as new command shapes emerge; the gating responsibility moves entirely to `ask` (mutating verbs) and `deny` (structurally unsafe shapes)."
msgstr "Wildcard bakar batek ordezkatzen du 15+ pershape sarrerak (`* make *`, `docker *`, `gh api *`, `grep *`, `head *`, `tail *`, `tee *`, `wc *`, `echo *`, `pkill *`, `* > /tmp/*`, `*=* python* *`, `gh issue *`, `gh run *`, `make *`) hori hondar-kutxaren atzeraldi heuristiko auto-allowrako itzulinguru gisa baino ez zegoen, enb aurrizkietan, birbideratzeetan, hodietan eta arg aipatuetan. Zurekin `Bash(*)` baimen-zerrenda ez da gehiago ustelduko komando-forma berriak sortzen diren heinean; erantzukizuna erabat mugitzen da `ask` (aditz mutatzaileak) eta `deny` (egiturazko forma seguruak)."

