# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "By default — for an **untrusted** fork PR — the privileged `pull_request_target` build checks out the **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) from the base repository: the PR's changes merged onto base, with all workflow and build-orchestration scripts coming from base, never from the fork. Because `actions/checkout` otherwise refuses to fetch a PR ref under `pull_request_target`, the source checkout sets `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. The untrusted build runs **without organization secrets** — `secrets: inherit` is not passed and it authenticates to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` only, so a malicious fork cannot read repository/organization secrets. (The `pull_request_target` token still carries `packages: write`, so the `🛡️ Trusted` label remains the real trust boundary for anything beyond image publication.)"
msgstr "Lehenespenez, batentzat **Konfiantzarik gabe** fork PR - pribilegiatua `pull_request_target` eraiki kontrolak **oinarri-konbinazioa** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) Oinarrizko biltegitik: PRen aldaketak oinarrira batu ziren, oinarritik datozen lan-fluxu eta muntaketa-script guztiak, inoiz ez sardexkatik. Zergatik? `actions/checkout` bestela uko egiten dio PR errefrente bat hartzeari `pull_request_target`, iturburuko kontrol-multzoak `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. **erakunde sekreturik gabe** - `secrets: inherit` ez da pasatzen eta GHCR-ra autentifikatzen du lan-ordukoarekin `GITHUB_TOKEN` bakarrik, beraz, sardexka maltzur batek ezin ditu biltegiaren eta antolaketaren sekretuak irakurri. (The `pull_request_target` tokenak jarraitzen du `packages: write`, beraz, `🛡️ Trusted` etiketa da irudiaren argitalpenetik kanpo dagoen guztiaren benetako muga.)"

