msgid "Each check requires a nonempty text answer and requests at most ``services.litellm.validation.max_output_tokens`` (512) output tokens. This allows reasoning models to produce visible text after their internal reasoning and can incur an API charge. Provider checks run concurrently in isolated Python processes, keeping each SDK’s redirected output and logging independent. It uses ``services.litellm.upstream_timeout`` and does not retry failed requests. Logs contain provider/model labels, HTTP status and a sanitized diagnostic; credentials and raw provider errors are never printed. A successful check proves that the key can make that model request at deploy time, not that future quota, availability or a large Claude conversation will fit. Subscription billing is separate and is not validated by these tasks."
msgstr ""

