msgid "On a Tor node the node dnsmasq resolves ``.onion`` through Tor's DNSPort and everything else through the clearnet upstream, which is what makes per-app proxy settings unnecessary. It is only reachable on the docker bridge address because docker discards loopback resolvers, and it is absent before docker itself is installed, hence the guard."
msgstr "Tor nodo batean dnsmasq nodoa ebazten da ``.onion`` Tor-en DNSPort-en bidez eta beste guztia korronte garbiaren bidez, hau da, aplikazio bakoitzeko proxy-ezarpenak ez dira beharrezkoak. Docker zubiaren helbidera bakarrik iristen da, docker-ek begizta-ebakitzaileak baztertzen dituelako, eta ez da falta docker-a bera instalatuta egon aurretik, beraz zaindaria."

msgid "On a consuming host every consumer uses the mesh URL and the host's key, so no consumer role carries a branch of its own. Inventory provisioning leaves `svc-ai-litellm` out of such a host, and a host that carries it while naming a gateway host fails its deploy. The mesh publish is a compose feature: in swarm the engine does not honour a bind address, so a swarm gateway host does not answer on its mesh address."
msgstr ""

msgid "On a consuming host every consumer uses the mesh URL and the host’s key, so no consumer role carries a branch of its own. Inventory provisioning leaves ``svc-ai-litellm`` out of such a host, and a host that carries it while naming a gateway host fails its deploy. The mesh publish is a compose feature: in swarm the engine does not honour a bind address, so a swarm gateway host does not answer on its mesh address."
