# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk does not open LDAP connections itself. It relies on Keycloak's LDAP federation (`svc-db-openldap` is mapped into the central Keycloak realm) and queries Keycloak's admin Web API for user lookups. This avoids dual-source-of-truth problems and keeps LDAP credentials away from the OpenTalk service account."
msgstr "OpenTalk-ek ez ditu LDAP konexioak irekitzen. Keycloak-en LDAP federazioan oinarritzen da. (`svc-db-openldap` Keycloak erreinu zentralean mapatuta dago) eta galdetu Keycloak-en web API-a erabiltzaile-bilaketarako. Honek iturburu bikoitzeko arazoak saihesten ditu eta LDAP kredentzialak OpenTalk zerbitzutik kanpo mantentzen ditu."

msgid "OpenTalk has no administrator role: controller migration `V21__remove_administrator_role.sql` removed it, and no claim grants elevated rights. The web frontend requests the fixed scopes `openid profile email`, so the `phone` scope is never requested, and the controller stores `phone_number` only when a `[call_in]` section is configured."
