msgid "Shared sign-in budget: `POST /api/auth/token` allows 5 attempts per 15 minutes per `request.remote`, and the app ignores `X-Forwarded-For`, so every browser behind the front proxy and the deploy's own token request share one bucket (measured: all logins in `/api/admin/auth-audit` come from `192.168.75.1`). At 2026.10.11 the budget is the module constant `AUTH_TOKEN_RATE_LIMIT` in `socialhome/routes/users.py` with no env or TOML key, and `trusted_proxies` exists for the GFS only (`socialhome/global_server/config.py`); the design spec keeps one administrator token in the Playwright staging volume. Options: let the proxy reach the app with the client address (PROXY protocol or upstream trusted-proxy support), or ask upstream to honour a trusted forwarded header."
