msgid "The role checks whether `pip` from `ansible_python_interpreter` supports `--break-system-packages` and only uses it (plus `PIP_BREAK_SYSTEM_PACKAGES=1`) when available. This keeps the role compatible with older `pip` versions (e.g., some CentOS/RHEL systems)."
msgstr "Rolak egiaztatzen du ea `pip` - `ansible_python_interpreter` euskarria `--break-system-packages` eta soilik erabiltzen du (plus `PIP_BREAK_SYSTEM_PACKAGES=1`) erabilgarri dagoenean. Honek zahartzaroarekin bateragarria izaten jarraitzen du. `pip` bertsioak (adibidez, CentOS/RHEL sistema batzuk.)."

msgid "The role comes from ``APP_ID``, which the deploy workflow sets to the row's app and :mod:`cli.administration.deploy.development.deploy.run` forwards into the container. A round that carries no such name, or one naming a role that publishes no guide, draws an invokable peer at random instead, so a local round covers a different guide each time rather than always the first one the inventory happens to list. Invokability comes from :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, so no caller re-derives it from role-name prefixes."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
