# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`, see [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) bounds every write, every read, and every outbound connection. `deny` rules block destructive patterns unconditionally; `ask` rules force operator review on every mutating `gh`/`docker`/`git commit`/`Skill(update-config*)` invocation. The wildcard does **not** loosen any existing guardrail; it only drops the per-shape workarounds."
msgstr "Sandbox (`allowWrite`, `denyRead`, `allowedDomains`, Ikusi [sandbox.md](sandbox.md)) idazketa bakoitza, irakurketa bakoitza eta konexio guztiak mugatzen ditu. `deny` arau-bloke suntsitzaileak baldintzarik gabe; `ask` mutazio bakoitzeko arauen eragilearen berrikuspena `gh`/`docker`/`git commit`/`Skill(update-config*)` Deia. Basatiak egiten du **ez** Existitzen den edozein guardasola askatzen du; per-shape-konponketa besterik ez du egiten."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox `denyRead: ~/.gnupg` rule blocks GPG access by design; agent commands must never touch private key material. This env override removes the resulting signing failure without weakening the credential-path protection. Agent-authored commits land unsigned; the `Co-Authored-By` trailer documents authorship."
msgstr "Sandbox `denyRead: ~/.gnupg` erregelak GPGren sarbidea diseinuz blokeatzen du; agenteen komandoek ez dute inoiz gako pribatuaren materiala ukitu behar. Inbestidura horrek emaitzaren sinaduraren hutsegitea ezabatzen du kredentzialaren bide-babesa ahuldu gabe. Agenteak sinatu gabeko lurra egiten du; `Co-Authored-By` trailer dokumentuen egilea."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox can connect to any Unix-domain socket on the host. Required so commands like `docker`, `systemctl`, and language servers continue to work; these all communicate over Unix sockets (e.g. `/var/run/docker.sock`)."
msgstr "Sandbox-a ostalariko Unix-domeinuko edozein socket-ekin konekta daiteke. Beharrezkoak dira, beraz, aginduak `docker`, `systemctl`, eta hizkuntza-zerbitzariek lanean jarraitzen dute; hauek guztiak Unix socket-en bidez komunikatzen dira. (Adibidez: `/var/run/docker.sock`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox cannot be escaped through the host daemon"
msgstr "Sandbox ezin da ihes egin ostalariaren daemon-aren bidez"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sandbox has `sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets: true` so that normal workflow tools (`docker`, `systemctl`, language servers) continue to work. Any command that reaches `/var/run/docker.sock` can request a container with `-v /:/host --privileged`, which the Docker daemon executes as root and mounts the host filesystem. The sandbox's `allowWrite` does NOT protect against this path because Docker is a trusted service on the other end of the socket."
msgstr "Harea-kutxak badu `sandbox.network.allowAllUnixSockets: true` beraz, lan-fluxuaren tresna normalak (`docker`, `systemctl`, Hizkuntza-zerbitzariak) Segi lanean. Edozein komando iristen da `/var/run/docker.sock` edukiontzi bat eska dezake `-v /:/host --privileged`, Docker daemon-ak erro gisa exekutatzen du eta ostalari-sistema muntatzen du. Harea-kutxa `allowWrite` Ez du bide horretatik babesten Docker konfiantzazko zerbitzua delako socket-aren beste muturrean."

# `"sandbox": { "enabled": true }`. Honek esan nahi du fitxategi-sistema eta
# sare-mugak behean betearazten direla **saio guztietan**, ez bakarrik
# operadorea eskuz sandbox baimen modura aldatzen denean. OS mailako
# harea-kutxa egia-iturria da komandoak irakurri, idatzi eta sarean zehar
# iristeko; `allow`/`ask`/`deny` Baimen-zerrendak indarrean jarraitzen dute,
# S.E.ri buruzko politiken bigarren defentsa-lerro gisa. (adibidez,
# baieztapena eskatzen du argitaratu aurretik.).
# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The sandbox is activated unconditionally via `\"sandbox\": { \"enabled\": true }`. This means filesystem and network restrictions below are enforced **at every session**, not only when the operator manually switches into sandbox permission mode. The OS-level sandbox is the source of truth for what commands may read, write, and reach over the network; the `allow`/`ask`/`deny` permission lists remain in force as a second line of defence for policy concerns the OS cannot express (e.g. requiring confirmation before publishing a commit)."
msgstr "Harea-kutxa baldintzarik gabe aktibatzen da bidez `\"sandbox\": { \"enabled\": true }`. Honek esan nahi du fitxategi-sistema eta sare-mugak behean betearazten direla **saio guztietan**, ez bakarrik operadorea eskuz sandbox baimen modura aldatzen denean. OS mailako harea-kutxa egia-iturria da komandoak irakurri, idatzi eta sarean zehar iristeko; `allow`/`ask`/`deny` Baimen-zerrendak indarrean jarraitzen dute, S.E.ri buruzko politiken bigarren defentsa-lerro gisa. (adibidez, baieztapena eskatzen du argitaratu aurretik.)."

msgid "The sandbox's `denyRead` list (`~/.aws`, `~/.config/gcloud`, `~/.docker/config.json`, `~/.git-credentials`, `~/.gnupg`, `~/.kube`, `~/.netrc`, and the default private keys under `~/.ssh`) is the primary mechanism that prevents the agent from reading host credentials. Every credential store an operator uses on the host is assumed to be covered, **with the documented exceptions of the rest of `~/.ssh`** (see Assumption 10) **and `~/.config/gh`**, which `gh` needs on every call."
msgstr ""

msgid "The scan is a stdlib line parse rather than a YAML load. This module is imported by the ``.env`` generator, which runs on the bare bootstrap python before any dependency is installed, so it must not reach PyYAML - directly or through ``utils.cache.yaml``. Only the ``image:`` value is needed and it is always a plain scalar, so a line match is sufficient; a value carrying Jinja is skipped, because its registry is not knowable before the templar runs."
