msgid "Until the swarm proof below passes, a swarm deploy with `services.openldap.network.public: true` is refused in two places. `svc-db-openldap` stops right after its run-once flag, before any other task of the role. `stream_relay_active` raises for a switch that is on in a mode of `UNPROVEN_STREAM_RELAY_MODES` (today `swarm`), so every network lookup of openresty and openldap fails: openresty's compose render, the relay pre-create and every `proxy_hops` lookup included. A play that runs openresty without openldap therefore never creates the relay network, never joins it and never publishes 636, so a failing relay task cannot take down the front proxy. Both messages name the switch and this requirement by its title, because a lint forbids requirement numbers and paths in code. The change that ticks the swarm proof removes both refusals and their tests. Compose deploys never hit either."
