# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "You MUST describe only the current state of the subject. You MUST NOT carry historical context, migration notes, or comparisons to former implementations into documentation. Phrases such as \"this replaces X\", \"previously X did Y\", \"formerly known as X\", \"the legacy X\", or \"after the refactor\" MUST NOT appear in documentation. Readers arrive in the present and need to know how the subject works now, not how it used to work. Historical context belongs in commit messages, pull request descriptions, and changelogs, where it is anchored to a point in time and ages gracefully. Documentation that carries history rots as soon as the next refactor lands."
msgstr "Gaiaren uneko egoera bakarrik deskribatu behar duzu. Ez duzu testuinguru historikoa, migrazio-oharrak edo aurreko inplementazioak dokumentaziora eraman behar. Esaldiak, adibidez \"honek X ordezkatzen du\", \"lehenago X-k Y-ri\", \"lehenago X izenez ezaguna\", \"X ondarea\"edo \"fabrikaren ondoren\" Ez da dokumentazioan agertu behar. Irakurleak orainera iristen dira eta jakin behar dute nola funtzionatzen duen gaiak, ez nola funtzionatzen zuen. Testuinguru historikoa konpromiso-mezuetan dago, eskaera-azalpenetan eta aldaketa-logetan, non denbora eta adin tarte batean ainguratzen den. Historia daraman dokumentazioa hurrengo errefektorea lurreratu bezain laster usteltzen da."

