msgstr "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_FRONTEND_IP` env var, barne-osagaietarako"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_MAX_AGE_MIN` (default `8640` = 6 days) controls how long every Nexus proxy repo holds an upstream response before revalidating. The bootstrap helper applies it as `contentMaxAge`, `metadataMaxAge`, and `negativeCache.timeToLive`. The default is intentionally one day below the 7-day `Valid-Until` window Debian and Ubuntu generate in their apt `Release` files, so Nexus always refreshes the manifest before `apt-get update` would see it expired. Raise it for slow-moving upstreams when staleness is preferable to upstream load; lower it further for fast-moving feeds (`apt-debian-security`, branch-pinned tarballs) when staleness becomes visible."
msgstr "`INFINITO_CACHE_PACKAGE_MAX_AGE_MIN` (lehenetsia `8640` = 6 egun) kontrolak zenbat denbora behar duen Nexus proxy-aren repo bakoitzak korrontean gora erantzun bat jasotzeko berriro balioetsi aurretik. Bota-trapen laguntzaileak honela aplikatzen du: `contentMaxAge`, `metadataMaxAge`, eta `negativeCache.timeToLive`. Lehenetsia nahita dago egun bat beherago 7-Eguna `Valid-Until` Debian eta Ubuntu leihoak beren apetan sortzen dira `Release` fitxategiak, beraz, Nexus-ek beti freskatzen du aurreko manifestua `apt-get update` iraungita ikusiko litzateke. Igo poliki-poliki korronteetara stalenessa kargagarria denean; jaitsi aurrerago azkar mugitzen diren iturrietarako. (`apt-debian-security`, adardun tarbolak) Atsekabea ikusgai dagoenean."

