msgid "``biber`` holds no EspoCRM role group, and every sign-in path admits only role-group members: with ``sso`` the role-group OIDC user provider refuses it, with LDAP only ``ldapUserLoginFilter`` refuses it, and without either no ``biber`` account exists. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. ```files/playwright/test-rbac.js`` <./files/playwright/test-rbac.js>`__ asserts the refusal and adds ``biber`` to the ``user``, ``manager`` and ``administrator`` groups in turn to assert the rights each one grants. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr ""

msgid "``biber`` in each of the ``administrator``, ``manager``, ``publisher``, ``editor``, ``author`` and ``registered`` groups landing in the matching Joomla group, the bootstrap administrator keeping ``Super Users`` without the ``administrator`` group, and ``biber`` without a role group landing in ``Registered``, read from Users: Manage (```test-rbac-groups.js`` <./files/playwright/test-rbac-groups.js>`__);"
msgstr ""

msgid "``biber`` joins the ``auditor`` role group for its persona journey and opens the central dashboard; ``files/playwright/test-rbac.js`` proves that biber without a role group is refused. With ``sso`` disabled Grafana knows only the break-glass account, so ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` is ``true`` then."
msgstr ""

msgid "``biber`` runs in ``files/playwright/test-biber-persona.js`` while ``sso`` is enabled and is skipped with ``SSO_SERVICE_ENABLED=false``. Without a Flowise role group, the oauth2-proxy refuses ``biber`` with a 403 at ``/oauth2/callback``, because ``sso.oauth2.allowed_groups`` in ``meta/services.yml`` admits only the ``administrator`` and ``mcp`` role groups. In the ``mcp`` role group, ``biber`` passes the gate and lands on Flowise’s own sign-in form: the role grants no Flowise account, so the app shell stays absent and ``/api/v1/chatflows`` answers 401. The scenario joins ``biber`` to the group through the Keycloak Admin REST API and removes the membership afterwards."
msgstr ""

msgid "``biber`` runs in `files/playwright/test-biber-persona.js <./files/playwright/test-biber-persona.js>`__ while ``sso`` is enabled and is skipped with ``SSO_SERVICE_ENABLED=false``, where the only credential left belongs to no user account. The oauth2-proxy admits only the application’s administrator RBAC group, so the scenario asserts that ``biber`` is refused with a 403 at ``/oauth2/callback``, stays on that refusal and receives no Postmarks ``connect.sid`` session."
msgstr ""

