msgid "`files/playwright/test-multisite-rbac.js` checks the member's own site with the protocol of the pass's base URL (`:78`, `:92`, `:112`, `:146`): on the Tor pass that is `http://` on an onion base, while own sites exist only on the regular network with TLS (served names get no onion sibling), and the own-site login redirect host at `:159` and the `maxRedirects: 0` POST at `:134-139` expect the onion network. Measured in `/tmp/compose-deploy-iam-20.log`; the SOCKS failure of the same spec is fixed by the served domains in `plugins/lookup/browser_proxy_bypass.py`. Options: render `WORDPRESS_SITE_OWNER_BASE_URL` into `templates/playwright.env.j2` from the served name through `lookup('tls', …)` and check own sites on their own network in every pass, or skip the own-site checks on the Tor pass."
