msgid "`tasks/utils/objectfs.yml` copies the plugin from the image into the persistent code volume, runs `admin/cli/upgrade.php`, then writes `MOODLE_OBJECTFS_READY_FILE` into the code volume and purges the caches. `files/build/config.php` names `alternative_file_system_class` only once that file exists, so `install_database.php` and the plugin's own upgrade run on Moodle's default file system. The plugin directory is not usable as that signal: `files/build/moodle-entrypoint.sh` copies the whole image tree into the code volume at container start, before any Ansible task runs."
