msgid "🚪 **Login Methods:** ``services.taiga.login.method.*`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ drives Taiga’s own switches. ``sso`` installs and configures the OIDC plugin (together with the ``sso`` service). ``ldap`` installs ``taiga-contrib-ldap-auth-ext`` and sets ``loginFormType: ldap`` (together with the ``ldap`` service), so under SSO LDAP accounts sign in through the Keycloak federation. ``native`` or ``ldap`` sets ``defaultLoginEnabled`` in the front’s ``conf.json``, which shows the username and password form with its “Forgot it?” link; with ``ldap`` on the form authenticates against the directory, so it is a shared form for both. ``registration`` sets ``publicRegisterEnabled`` in ``conf.json`` and ``PUBLIC_REGISTER_ENABLED`` for the backend. Taiga has no second factor or passkey, so the role declares neither."
msgstr ""

msgid "🚪 **Login Methods:** `services.taiga.login.method.*` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml) drives Taiga's own switches. `sso` installs and configures the OIDC plugin (together with the `sso` service). `ldap` installs `taiga-contrib-ldap-auth-ext` and sets `loginFormType: ldap` (together with the `ldap` service), so under SSO LDAP accounts sign in through the Keycloak federation. `native` or `ldap` sets `defaultLoginEnabled` in the front's `conf.json`, which shows the username and password form with its \"Forgot it?\" link; with `ldap` on the form authenticates against the directory, so it is a shared form for both. `registration` sets `publicRegisterEnabled` in `conf.json` and `PUBLIC_REGISTER_ENABLED` for the backend. Taiga has no second factor or passkey, so the role declares neither."
msgstr ""

